course: dictionary
lesson: 13661
title: Words that flow in
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words hide clues inside them. Inflowing is built from in and flowing. Flowing means moving along like water, and in means into. So inflowing means flowing into a place. «The inflowing streams feed the lake.» The streams flow into the lake and keep it full.
explain: Read the words around it to check. «The inflowing tide covered the sand within an hour.» The tide is the sea coming in, and covering the sand tells you it is moving onto the beach. Ask yourself: what is coming into what? Then put your meaning into the sentence instead of the hard word and see if it still makes sense.
explain: The word can also describe things that are not water. «Inflowing traffic jammed the bridge.» Cars are not flowing like water, but they are arriving in a steady stream, so the word still fits. «The inflowing money helped the school buy new books.» Money can arrive in a steady stream too.
explain: In maths, a tank problem may say: «Water is inflowing at 5 litres a minute.» The water is going into the tank, so the tank is filling up. When you see inflowing, look for what is going into a place, and you will be close to the meaning.
fact: Inflowing means flowing in, or coming into a place.
fact: «Inflowing» is an adjective, and it comes from the rare verb «inflow».
fact: «Inflowing» can describe water, air, tides, traffic or money arriving in a place in a stream.
fact: In geography, «inflowing rivers» are rivers that flow into a lake or sea.
fact: Common phrases are inflowing river, inflowing water and inflowing tide.
exercise: «The inflowing streams feed the lake.» What does inflowing mean here? | *Flowing into a place | Frozen solid | Dried up | Flowing out of the lake
exercise: «Inflowing traffic jammed the bridge.» What is arriving in a steady stream? | Clouds | Leaves | Fish | *Cars and lorries
exercise: Which phrase names water coming into a lake? | A dry riverbed | *An inflowing river | A frozen puddle | A sandy beach
test: «The inflowing tide covered the sand within an hour.» What does an inflowing tide mean? | A dry beach | The sea going out | *The sea coming in | A tide that has stopped
test: «Water is inflowing at 5 litres a minute.» What is happening to the tank? | *It is filling up | It is frozen | It is emptying | It is drying out
exam: Sam says inflowing means going out. Is Sam right? | Only true for rivers | Yes, it means going out | It means still and calm | *No, it means flowing into a place
